; bal -X EUR --unrealized foots to zero when an --account-rewrite or
; --payee-rewrite option, rather than a directive, gives the rewrite rule:
; rewrite_posts copies a transaction it rewrites once, whole, keeping its
; date, whichever gives the rule, so the report values the costs of both
; postings on the transaction's date, as it does without a rule.  The
; journal is that of unrealized-footing-posting-date.test; the output is
; that of unrealized-account-rewrite.test and unrealized-payee-rewrite.test,
; which give the same rules by directive.

P 2024/01/01 $ 0.90 EUR
P 2024/01/10 $ 0.80 EUR

2024/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL @ $150  ; [2024/01/15]
    Assets:Checking

P 2024/03/05 AAPL $170

test bal -X EUR --unrealized --account-rewrite Brokerage=Assets:Broker
           EUR160.00  Assets
          EUR1360.00    Broker
         EUR-1200.00    Checking
          EUR-160.00  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -X EUR --unrealized --payee-rewrite Buy=Purchase
           EUR160.00  Assets
          EUR1360.00    Brokerage
         EUR-1200.00    Checking
          EUR-160.00  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test
